	section
		h3 Colors in Reveal
		p.small Standard Reveal themes give the arrows the same color that it uses for links. In this theme it is very blue.
		p.small Reveal also defines what color the controls should be on slides where the user has set another background color: If that background color is very dark, the controls become white, and if it is very light, the controls become black.

	section
		h3 Colors in Smallcontrol
		p.small Smallcontrol keeps the color your theme gives the arrows, the color of its links.
		p.small Only on slides that contrast the theme does it do something different: there the arrows get the color of the text on that slide, instead of plain black or white, like Reveal normally does. For an example, see #[a(href="#/2") light slide] in this deck.

	section
		h3 Your own colors
		p.small If you still want other colors, set them for regular slides and/or for slides that contrast the theme:

		pre
			code.hljs.javascript(data-line-numbers).
				Reveal.initialize({
					//...
					smallcontrol: {
						color: 'orange',
						inversecolor: 'darkred'
					},
					plugins: [ Smallcontrol ]
				})

	section
		h3 Scaling
		p.small Reveal always shows the controls at the same size, no matter how large the screen is. On a big screen that might be small and far away.
		p.small With #[code autoscale], you can let Smallcontrol grow along with the slides, up to twice their size, or whatever you set as a maximum with #[code maxscale]. This deck has it on: make the window larger to see it.

		pre
			code.hljs.javascript(data-line-numbers).
				Reveal.initialize({
					//...
					smallcontrol: {
						autoscale: true,
						maxscale: 2
					},
					plugins: [ Smallcontrol ]
				})

	section
		h3 The stylesheet
		p.small Smallcontrol loads its own stylesheet. If you import it yourself, set #[code csspath: false], or point #[code csspath] at your own file.

		pre
			code.hljs.javascript(data-line-numbers).
				import Smallcontrol from 'reveal.js-smallcontrol';
				import 'reveal.js-smallcontrol/smallcontrol.css';

